@[expose] public section

/-!
# Smoothness at a prime with separable residue field is regularity

Proof of Stacks 00TV. Let `k` be a field, let `S` be a finite type `k`-algebra and let `𝔮 ⊆ S` be
a prime whose residue field `κ = κ(𝔮)` is separable over `k`. Write `R = S_𝔮` for the local ring,
with maximal ideal `𝔪`. Then `S` is smooth at `𝔮` over `k` if and only if `R` is regular.

Smoothness always implies regularity, which is the `moreover` of Lemma 00TT. For the converse the
dimension of the fibre of the differentials is estimated: the conormal sequence
`𝔪/𝔪² → Ω_{R/k} ⊗_R κ → Ω_{κ/k} → 0` of Stacks 00RU is exact, so
`dim_κ Ω_{R/k} ⊗_R κ ≤ dim_κ 𝔪/𝔪² + dim_κ Ω_{κ/k}`, while `Ω_{R/k} ⊗_R κ = Ω_{S/k} ⊗_S κ`
because differentials localize (Lemma 00RT). Regularity of `R` makes `dim_κ 𝔪/𝔪² = dim R`, and
separability of `κ` makes `dim_κ Ω_{κ/k} ≤ trdeg_k κ`, so
`dim_κ Ω_{S/k} ⊗_S κ ≤ dim R + trdeg_k κ = dim_𝔮 S` by Lemma 00P1, which is the second condition
of Lemma 00TT.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Smooth.SeparableResidueRegular.solution`: the statement of Stacks 00TV, namely
  `Algebra.isSmoothAt_iff_isRegularLocalRing`.

## Implementation notes

The whole converse is carried by one estimate,
`finrank_tensor_kaehlerDifferential_le_height_add_trdeg`:
`dim_κ (κ ⊗_S Ω_{S/k}) ≤ height 𝔮 + trdeg_k κ(𝔮)` for a prime with regular local ring and
separable residue field. Lemma 00P1 identifies the right-hand side with `dim_𝔮 S`, so this is
verbatim the second condition of Lemma 00TT, and `solution` is that condition plus 00TT.

The source's dimension count is an equality, resting on injectivity of `d : 𝔪/𝔪² → Ω_{R/k} ⊗_R κ`,
which is Lemma 00TU. Only the inequality `≤` is used here, because the three conditions of Lemma
00TT are equivalent and the second of them is itself an inequality; the injectivity is what the
implication from smoothness to regularity needs, and that arrives through Lemma 00TT's `moreover`.

The conormal estimate is read off Mathlib's exact sequence
`KaehlerDifferential.exact_mapBaseChange_map`, whose right-hand map is surjective: the fibre modulo
the image of `𝔪/𝔪²` is `Ω_{κ/k}`, and the image has dimension at most `dim_κ 𝔪/𝔪²`. The dimension
count itself is `finrank_le_add_of_exact`, stated for an arbitrary right-exact sequence of
`κ`-modules whose left-hand map is merely `R`-linear: that is all
`KaehlerDifferential.kerCotangentToTensor` provides, and an `R`-linear map between `κ`-modules is
`κ`-linear because `R → κ` is surjective (`LinearMap.extendScalarsOfSurjective`).

`dim_κ Ω_{κ/k} ≤ trdeg_k κ` for a finitely generated separable extension `κ/k` is
`finrank_kaehlerDifferential_le_trdeg`. A separating transcendence basis `s` of `κ/k` makes `κ`
separable algebraic, hence formally unramified, over `L = k(s)`, so `Ω_{κ/L} = 0` and the same
exact sequence makes `κ ⊗_L Ω_{L/k} → Ω_{κ/k}` surjective; and `Ω_{L/k}` is generated by
`{d x | x ∈ s}` because `L` is the fraction field of `k[s]`, whose differentials are generated by
the differentials of its generators. The source states equality; the inequality is what is used
and it needs no freeness.

Five steps of that argument are not in Mathlib, so they are
proved here as private lemmas: `finrank_le_add_of_exact` above;
`KaehlerDifferential.span_image_D_of_adjoin_eq_top`, that `Ω_{S/R}` is spanned by the differentials
of any set of algebra generators of `S`; `KaehlerDifferential.span_range_map_D_adjoin_eq_top`, the
same statement for the intermediate field `k(s)`, which is the fraction field of `k[s]`, so that
differentials localize; `finrank_kaehlerDifferential_le_of_isSeparable`, that differentials do not
grow along a separable algebraic extension; and `Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated.of_algEquiv`, which
transports a separating transcendence basis along an isomorphism of extensions and so upgrades
separable generation of the subextension `⊤` to separable generation of `K` itself.

## References

* [Stacks 00TV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00TV)
* [Stacks 00P1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00P1)
* [Stacks 00RT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00RT)
* [Stacks 00RU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00RU)
* [Stacks 00TT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00TT)
* [Stacks 00TU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00TU)
-/

@[expose] public section

open Module TensorProduct KaehlerDifferential IsLocalRing

/-- **Dimension count for a right-exact sequence.** If `M →ₗ N →ₗ P` is exact with `N →ₗ P`
surjective, then `dim N ≤ dim M + dim P`. The left-hand map is only asked to be `R`-linear for a
ring `R` mapping onto the field `κ` of scalars: such a map between `κ`-modules is automatically
`κ`-linear, by `LinearMap.extendScalarsOfSurjective`. -/
private theorem finrank_le_add_of_exact {R κ M N P : Type*} [CommRing R] [Field κ] [Algebra R κ]
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module κ M] [IsScalarTower R κ M] [Module.Finite κ M]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [Module κ N] [IsScalarTower R κ N] [Module.Finite κ N]
    [AddCommGroup P] [Module κ P] (hRκ : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R κ))
    {f : M →ₗ[R] N} {g : N →ₗ[κ] P} (hfg : Function.Exact f g) (hg : Function.Surjective g) :
    finrank κ N ≤ finrank κ M + finrank κ P := by
  have hker : LinearMap.ker g = LinearMap.range (f.extendScalarsOfSurjective hRκ) :=
    LinearMap.exact_iff.mp hfg
  have h1 : finrank κ (LinearMap.ker g) ≤ finrank κ M := by
    rw [hker]; exact LinearMap.finrank_range_le _
  have h2 : finrank κ (N ⧸ LinearMap.ker g) = finrank κ P :=
    LinearEquiv.finrank_eq (g.quotKerEquivOfSurjective hg)
  have h3 := Submodule.finrank_quotient_add_finrank (R := κ) (LinearMap.ker g)
  omega

/-- The fibre at a prime of the module of differentials may be computed on the localization:
if `R` is a localization of the `k`-algebra `S` and `κ` is an `R`-algebra which is a field, then
`κ ⊗_S Ω_{S/k}` and `κ ⊗_R Ω_{R/k}` have the same dimension over `κ`. This is Stacks 00RT (2),
`omega_localization_total`, read after base change to `κ`. -/
private theorem finrank_tensor_kaehlerDifferential_eq_of_isLocalization
    (k S R κ : Type*) [Field k] [CommRing S] [CommRing R] [Field κ]
    [Algebra k S] [Algebra k R] [Algebra S R] [IsScalarTower k S R]
    (M : Submonoid S) [IsLocalization M R]
    [Algebra S κ] [Algebra R κ] [IsScalarTower S R κ] :
    finrank κ (κ ⊗[S] Ω[S⁄k]) = finrank κ (κ ⊗[R] Ω[R⁄k]) := by
  have hbc : IsBaseChange R (KaehlerDifferential.map k k S R) :=
    (isLocalizedModule_iff_isBaseChange M R _).mp (omega_localization_total k S M R)
  exact (LinearEquiv.finrank_eq
    ((AlgebraTensorModule.congr (LinearEquiv.refl κ κ) hbc.equiv.symm).trans
      (AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange S R κ κ Ω[S⁄k]))).symm

/-- **The conormal estimate.** For a Noetherian local `k`-algebra `R` with residue field `κ`, the
fibre `κ ⊗_R Ω_{R/k}` has dimension at most `dim_κ 𝔪/𝔪² + dim_κ Ω_{κ/k}`. This is exactness of
the conormal sequence of Stacks 00RU; the source's equality would in addition need injectivity on
`𝔪/𝔪²`, which is Stacks 00TU. -/
private theorem finrank_tensor_kaehlerDifferential_le_cotangentSpace_add
    (k R : Type*) [Field k] [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [Algebra k R]
    [Module.Finite R Ω[R⁄k]] :
    finrank (ResidueField R) (ResidueField R ⊗[R] Ω[R⁄k]) ≤
      finrank (ResidueField R) (CotangentSpace R)
        + finrank (ResidueField R) Ω[ResidueField R⁄k] := by
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R (ResidueField R)) := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  -- `kerCotangentToTensor` lives on `RingHom.ker (R → κ)`, which is `𝔪` only propositionally.
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ : ∃ d : (maximalIdeal R).Cotangent →ₗ[R] ResidueField R ⊗[R] Ω[R⁄k],
      Function.Exact d (mapBaseChange k R (ResidueField R)) := by
    rw [show maximalIdeal R = RingHom.ker (algebraMap R (ResidueField R)) from Ideal.mk_ker.symm]
    refine ⟨kerCotangentToTensor k R _, fun y ↦ ?_⟩
    rw [Set.mem_range, ← LinearMap.mem_range, range_kerCotangentToTensor k R _ hsurj]
    exact Iff.rfl
  exact finrank_le_add_of_exact hsurj hd (mapBaseChange_surjective k R _ hsurj)

/-- The module of differentials of an algebra is spanned by the differentials of any set of
algebra generators: if `Algebra.adjoin R s = ⊤` then `Ω[S⁄R]` is spanned over `S` by `d s`. -/
@[ega "0 20.4.7"]
private theorem KaehlerDifferential.span_image_D_of_adjoin_eq_top
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] {s : Set S}
    (hs : Algebra.adjoin R s = ⊤) :
    Submodule.span S (KaehlerDifferential.D R S '' s) = ⊤ := by
  set N := Submodule.span S (KaehlerDifferential.D R S '' s)
  -- `d` composed with `Ω[S⁄R] → Ω[S⁄R]/N` is a derivation vanishing on `s`, hence on `adjoin R s`.
  have h0 : Set.EqOn (N.mkQ.compDer (KaehlerDifferential.D R S)) 0 s := fun x hx ↦ by
    simpa [Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] using
      (Submodule.subset_span ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ : KaehlerDifferential.D R S x ∈ N)
  have h := Derivation.eqOn_adjoin (D1 := N.mkQ.compDer (KaehlerDifferential.D R S)) (D2 := 0) h0
  rw [eq_top_iff, ← span_range_derivation R S, Submodule.span_le]
  rintro x ⟨y, rfl⟩
  simpa [Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] using h (hs ▸ Algebra.mem_top (R := R) (x := y))

open scoped IntermediateField.algebraAdjoinAdjoin in
/-- The differentials of the subextension `k(s) ⊆ K` generated by a set `s` are spanned by the
differentials of the elements of `s`: `k(s)` is the fraction field of `k[s]`, and differentials
localize. -/
private theorem KaehlerDifferential.span_range_map_D_adjoin_eq_top
    {k K : Type*} [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K] (s : Set K) :
    Submodule.span (IntermediateField.adjoin k s)
      (Set.range fun x : s => KaehlerDifferential.map k k (Algebra.adjoin k s)
        (IntermediateField.adjoin k s)
          (KaehlerDifferential.D k (Algebra.adjoin k s) ⟨(x : K), Algebra.subset_adjoin x.2⟩)) =
      ⊤ := by
  set A := Algebra.adjoin k s
  set L := IntermediateField.adjoin k s
  have hι : (Set.range fun x : s ↦ (⟨(x : K), Algebra.subset_adjoin x.2⟩ : A))
      = ((↑) : A → K) ⁻¹' s :=
    Set.eq_of_subset_of_subset (fun _ ⟨x, hx⟩ ↦ hx ▸ x.2) fun a ha ↦ ⟨⟨a, ha⟩, rfl⟩
  rw [show (Set.range fun x : s ↦ KaehlerDifferential.map k k A L
        (KaehlerDifferential.D k A ⟨(x : K), Algebra.subset_adjoin x.2⟩))
      = KaehlerDifferential.map k k A L '' (KaehlerDifferential.D k A '' (((↑) : A → K) ⁻¹' s)) by
    rw [← hι, ← Set.range_comp, ← Set.range_comp]; rfl]
  exact _root_.span_eq_top_of_isLocalizedModule L (nonZeroDivisors A) _
    (span_image_D_of_adjoin_eq_top Algebra.adjoin_adjoin_coe_preimage)

/-- Differentials do not grow along a separable algebraic extension: if `K/L` is separable
algebraic then `dim_K Ω_{K/k} ≤ dim_L Ω_{L/k}`. Indeed `K` is formally unramified over `L`, so
`Ω_{K/L} = 0` and the exact sequence `K ⊗_L Ω_{L/k} → Ω_{K/k} → Ω_{K/L} → 0` of Stacks 00RU makes
`Ω_{K/k}` a quotient of `K ⊗_L Ω_{L/k}`. -/
private theorem finrank_kaehlerDifferential_le_of_isSeparable (k L K : Type*) [Field k] [Field L]
    [Field K] [Algebra k L] [Algebra k K] [Algebra L K] [IsScalarTower k L K]
    [Algebra.IsSeparable L K] [Module.Finite L Ω[L⁄k]] :
    finrank K Ω[K⁄k] ≤ finrank L Ω[L⁄k] := by
  have : Algebra.FormallyUnramified L K := Algebra.FormallyUnramified.of_isSeparable L K
  have : Subsingleton Ω[K⁄L] := Algebra.FormallyUnramified.subsingleton_kaehlerDifferential
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (KaehlerDifferential.mapBaseChange k L K) :=
    fun x ↦ (KaehlerDifferential.exact_mapBaseChange_map k L K x).mp (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  calc finrank K Ω[K⁄k] ≤ finrank K (K ⊗[L] Ω[L⁄k]) :=
        LinearMap.finrank_le_finrank_of_surjective hsurj
    _ = finrank L Ω[L⁄k] := Module.finrank_baseChange ..

open scoped IntermediateField.algebraAdjoinAdjoin in
/-- A separating transcendence basis `s` of `K/k` bounds the dimension of the differentials by the
transcendence degree: `Ω_{L/k}` is spanned by the `#s` differentials of the elements of `s`, where
`L = k(s)`, and `K` is separable algebraic over `L`, so `Ω_{K/k}` is no bigger. -/
private theorem finrank_kaehlerDifferential_le_trdeg_of_isTranscendenceBasis
    {k K : Type*} [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K] {s : Set K}
    (hs : IsTranscendenceBasis k ((↑) : s → K))
    (hsep : Algebra.IsSeparable (IntermediateField.adjoin k s) K) :
    (finrank K Ω[K⁄k] : ℕ∞) ≤ Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg k K) := by
  rcases Set.finite_or_infinite s with hfin | hinf
  · have := hfin.fintype
    set L := IntermediateField.adjoin k s
    have hspanL := KaehlerDifferential.span_range_map_D_adjoin_eq_top (k := k) s
    have : Module.Finite L Ω[L⁄k] :=
      Module.finite_def.mpr (Submodule.fg_def.mpr ⟨_, Set.finite_range _, hspanL⟩)
    calc (finrank K Ω[K⁄k] : ℕ∞)
        ≤ (Fintype.card s : ℕ∞) :=
          Nat.cast_le.mpr ((finrank_kaehlerDifferential_le_of_isSeparable k L K).trans
            (finrank_le_of_span_eq_top hspanL))
      _ = Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg k K) := by rw [← hs.cardinalMk_eq_trdeg]; simp
  · rw [← hs.cardinalMk_eq_trdeg,
      Cardinal.toENat_eq_top.mpr (Cardinal.infinite_iff.mp hinf.to_subtype)]
    exact le_top

/-- Separable generation, Definition 030O (1), only depends on the extension up to isomorphism:
a separating transcendence basis transports along an isomorphism `K ≃ₐ[k] K'`. -/
private theorem Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated.of_algEquiv {k K K' : Type*} [Field k] [Field K]
    [Field K'] [Algebra k K] [Algebra k K'] [Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated k K] (e : K ≃ₐ[k] K') :
    Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated k K' := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hsep⟩ :=
    Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated.isSeparable (k := k) (K := K)
  have hmap : (IntermediateField.adjoin k s).map (e : K →ₐ[k] K')
      = IntermediateField.adjoin k (e '' s) := IntermediateField.adjoin_map k s _
  refine ⟨e '' s, (e.isTranscendenceBasis hs).to_subtype_range'
    (by rw [Set.range_comp, Subtype.range_coe]), ?_⟩
  exact Algebra.IsSeparable.of_equiv_equiv
    ((IntermediateField.intermediateFieldMap e (IntermediateField.adjoin k s)).trans
      (IntermediateField.equivOfEq hmap)).toRingEquiv e.toRingEquiv (by ext x; rfl)

/-- For a finitely generated separable field extension `K/k` — separability in the sense of
Definition 030O (2) — the module of differentials has dimension at most the transcendence degree.
The extension is one of its own finitely generated subextensions, so separable generation of `⊤`
transports to `K`. -/
private theorem finrank_kaehlerDifferential_le_trdeg (k K : Type*) [Field k] [Field K]
    [Algebra k K] [Algebra.EssFiniteType k K] [Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k K] :
    (finrank K Ω[K⁄k] : ℕ∞) ≤ Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg k K) := by
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType k (⊤ : IntermediateField k K) :=
    (Algebra.EssFiniteType.iff_of_algEquiv
      (IntermediateField.topEquiv (F := k) (E := K))).mpr inferInstance
  have : Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated k K :=
    .of_algEquiv (IntermediateField.topEquiv (F := k) (E := K))
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hsep⟩ :=
    Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated.isSeparable (k := k) (K := K)
  exact finrank_kaehlerDifferential_le_trdeg_of_isTranscendenceBasis hs hsep

/-- **The fibre estimate that carries Stacks 00TV.** For a prime `𝔮` of a finite type `k`-algebra
`S` whose residue field is separable over `k` and whose local ring is regular,
`dim_κ (κ ⊗_S Ω_{S/k}) ≤ height 𝔮 + trdeg_k κ(𝔮)`. By Lemma 00P1 the right-hand side is the local
dimension `dim_𝔮 S`, so this is the second condition of Lemma 00TT. -/
private theorem finrank_tensor_kaehlerDifferential_le_height_add_trdeg
    {k S : Type*} [Field k] [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S] (I : Ideal S)
    [I.IsPrime] [Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k I.ResidueField]
    (hreg : IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime I)) :
    (finrank I.ResidueField (I.ResidueField ⊗[S] Ω[S⁄k]) : ℕ∞)
      ≤ I.height + Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg k I.ResidueField) := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing (Localization.AtPrime I) := hreg.toIsNoetherian
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType k (Localization.AtPrime I) :=
    Algebra.EssFiniteType.comp k S (Localization.AtPrime I)
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType k I.ResidueField :=
    Algebra.EssFiniteType.comp k (Localization.AtPrime I) I.ResidueField
  have hdim : (finrank I.ResidueField (CotangentSpace (Localization.AtPrime I)) : ℕ∞)
      = I.height := by
    have h := (IsRegularLocalRing.iff_finrank_cotangentSpace (Localization.AtPrime I)).mp hreg
    rw [IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height I (Localization.AtPrime I)] at h
    exact_mod_cast h
  rw [finrank_tensor_kaehlerDifferential_eq_of_isLocalization k S (Localization.AtPrime I)
    I.ResidueField I.primeCompl]
  calc (finrank I.ResidueField
          (I.ResidueField ⊗[Localization.AtPrime I] Ω[Localization.AtPrime I⁄k]) : ℕ∞)
      ≤ (finrank I.ResidueField (CotangentSpace (Localization.AtPrime I)) : ℕ∞)
          + (finrank I.ResidueField Ω[I.ResidueField⁄k] : ℕ∞) := by
        exact_mod_cast finrank_tensor_kaehlerDifferential_le_cotangentSpace_add k
          (Localization.AtPrime I)
    _ ≤ I.height + Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg k I.ResidueField) := by
        rw [hdim]; exact add_le_add le_rfl (finrank_kaehlerDifferential_le_trdeg k I.ResidueField)

namespace Stacks.Smooth.SeparableResidueRegular

/-- Let `S` be a finite type algebra over a field `k` and `q` a prime of `S` whose residue field is
separable over `k`. Then `S` is smooth over `k` at `q` if and only if the localization `S_q` is a
regular local ring. -/
public theorem solution
    {k S : Type*} [Field k] [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S]
    (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] [Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k q.ResidueField]
    (Sq : Type*) [CommRing Sq] [Algebra S Sq] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq q] :
    Algebra.IsSmoothAt k q ↔ IsRegularLocalRing Sq := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ : ∃ x : PrimeSpectrum S, x.asIdeal = q := ⟨⟨q, ‹q.IsPrime›⟩, rfl⟩
  have H := Algebra.isSmoothAt_tfae_localKrullDim_and_isRegularLocalRing (k := k) x Sq
  refine ⟨H.2, fun hreg ↦ (H.1.out 2 1).mp ?_⟩
  rw [PrimeSpectrum.localKrullDim_eq_height_add_trdeg_residueField k x]
  exact_mod_cast finrank_tensor_kaehlerDifferential_le_height_add_trdeg x.asIdeal
    (IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv
      (IsLocalization.algEquiv x.asIdeal.primeCompl Sq
        (Localization.AtPrime x.asIdeal)).toRingEquiv)

end Stacks.Smooth.SeparableResidueRegular

end

/-!
# Smoothness at a prime with separable residue field is regularity

Let `k` be a field, let `S` be a finite type `k`-algebra and let `𝔮 ⊆ S` be a prime whose residue
field `κ(𝔮)` is separable over `k`. Then `S` is smooth at `𝔮` over `k` if and only if the local
ring `S_𝔮` is regular.

Over an arbitrary field smoothness at `𝔮` is strictly stronger than regularity of `S_𝔮`: by
Lemma 00TT it says that the fibre `Ω_{S/k} ⊗_S κ(𝔮)` has exactly the local dimension of `Spec S`
at `𝔮`, whereas regularity only says `dim_{κ(𝔮)} 𝔪/𝔪² = dim S_𝔮`. Separability of `κ(𝔮)` closes
the gap: writing `R = S_𝔮` with maximal ideal `𝔪` and residue field `κ`, Lemmas 00TU and 00RU give
a short exact sequence `0 → 𝔪/𝔪² → Ω_{R/k} ⊗_R κ → Ω_{κ/k} → 0`, and separability of `κ/k` makes
`dim_κ Ω_{κ/k} = trdeg_k κ`, so
`dim_κ (Ω_{R/k} ⊗_R κ) = dim_κ 𝔪/𝔪² + trdeg_k κ ≥ dim R + trdeg_k κ = dim_𝔮 S`
by Lemma 00P1, with equality exactly when `R` is regular.

Without separability the implication from regularity to smoothness fails: for `k = 𝐅_p(t)` and
`S = k[X]/(X^p - t)` the ring `S` is a field, so `S_𝔮` is regular at `𝔮 = 0`, while
`Ω_{S/k} = S dX` is nonzero over a zero-dimensional algebra and `S` is not smooth over `k`; here
`κ(𝔮) = k(t^{1/p})` is purely inseparable over `k`.

## Main results

* `Algebra.isSmoothAt_iff_isRegularLocalRing`: for a finite type algebra over a field, smoothness
  at a prime with separable residue field is regularity of the local ring at that prime.

## Implementation notes

Separability of `κ(𝔮)/k` is `Algebra.IsSeparableExtension k κ(𝔮)`, Definition 030O (2): every
subextension of `κ(𝔮)/k` that is finitely generated over `k` admits a transcendence basis over
which it is separable algebraic. It is *not* Mathlib's `Algebra.IsSeparable k κ(𝔮)`, which is
separability of an *algebraic* extension and would exclude the transcendental primes that are the
main application, such as the generic point of a variety; for an algebraic extension the only
transcendence basis is empty and the two agree. Being a class it is an instance hypothesis, so
instance search supplies it at the use sites.

The hypothesis is the source's separability, not the a priori weaker
`Algebra.IsSeparablyGenerated k κ(𝔮)` of Definition 030O (1): the two are equivalent here, since
`Algebra.FiniteType k S` makes `κ(𝔮)/k` finitely generated, but the equivalence is Lemma 030X, and
the sequence of Lemma 00TU is stated under the source's condition. `Algebra.EssFiniteType k κ(𝔮)`
is for the same reason not assumed even though the route through Lemma 00TU uses it.

The residue field `κ(𝔮)` is `Ideal.ResidueField 𝔮`, by definition the residue field of
`Localization.AtPrime 𝔮`, with its induced `k`-algebra structure. The local ring `S_𝔮` itself is
an arbitrary model `Sq`, pinned by `IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq 𝔮` as in the sibling 00TT, rather
than the fixed `Localization.AtPrime 𝔮`: regularity is invariant under the resulting isomorphism
and this is the form the consumers apply. Regularity is `IsRegularLocalRing`, Definition 00KU
(Definition 00OD is the global notion, `IsRegularRing`), and smoothness at `𝔮` is
`Algebra.IsSmoothAt k 𝔮`, formal smoothness of `Localization.AtPrime 𝔮` over `k`, which by
Lemma 00TA is the source's "there is `g ∉ 𝔮` with `S_g` smooth over `k`". The source's two-item
enumeration is an `Iff` rather than a `List.TFAE`.

Faithfulness to [Stacks 00TV], on the four points a reader should check.
(1) No hypothesis is dead: separability fails for the `𝐅_p(t)`-example above, where (2) holds and
(1) does not; `Algebra.FiniteType k S` fails for `ℚ[x₁, x₂, …]` at `(x₁, x₂, …)`, which is smooth
at `𝔮` while its local ring is not Noetherian, hence not a regular local ring; the base being a
field is what Lemma 00P1 needs, and over `ℤ` the algebra `𝐅_p` at `𝔮 = 0` has `S_𝔮` regular and
is not smooth; and `IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq 𝔮` is what makes `Sq` item (2)'s `S_𝔮`.
(2) The scalars and base are the source's: smoothness of `S` over `k`, regularity of `S_𝔮` itself,
and separability of `κ(𝔮)` over `k` — not over `S` or `S_𝔮`, and no base field extension appears.
(3) The canonical objects are pinned, not merely asserted to exist: `Sq` as a localization of `S`
at `𝔮` along `algebraMap S Sq`, `κ(𝔮)` as `Ideal.ResidueField 𝔮` over `k`, and smoothness at that
same prime `𝔮`; the intermediate *field* over which each finitely generated subextension is
separable algebraic is pinned inside Definition 030O.
(4) The instantiation is not degenerate and neither item is automatic: both hold for `k = ℚ`,
`S = ℚ[X]`, `𝔮 = (X)`, and for the transcendental prime `𝔮 = (X)` of `ℚ[X, Y]`, whose residue
field `ℚ(Y)` is separable over `ℚ` with transcendence basis `{Y}`; both fail for `S = ℚ[X, Y]/(XY)`
at `𝔮 = (X, Y)`, a node, whose residue field `ℚ` is separable over `ℚ`.

